<title>USA: First Midwest Bancorp Q3 net rises.</title>
<headline>First Midwest Bancorp Q3 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>ITASCA, Ill. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.63		   $ 0.56</p>
<p> Net			  8,602		    7,572</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q3 includes gain from bad debt recapture repeal which permitted reversal of a $992,000 after-tax charge recorded in the 1995 Q4 related to an acquisition. It also includes a one-time charge of $962,000 after taxes related to Savings Association Insurance Fund recapitalization.  </p>
<p>			9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.81		    $1.57</p>
<p> Net			 24,744		   21,317</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 nine months results included a nonrecurring $198,000 after-tax Citizens Federal acquisition credit that was recorded in the Q1. 1995's Q3, nine months included a nonrecurring $494,000 after-tax restructuring credit.</p>
<p>Assets $3.14 billion vs $3.27 billion</p>
<p>Deposits $2.30 billion vs $2.29 billion</p>
<p>Loans $1.97 billion vs $2.02 billion</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
